# The build context is the repository root for every image here (api, worker
# and web), so what is excluded below is excluded from all three.
#
# This file is not only about size. `COPY apps/web/ ./` in the web build would
# otherwise land the host's `node_modules` on top of the one `npm ci` just
# installed inside the image — native binaries built for the developer's
# platform, silently replacing the ones built for the image's.

.git/
.github/

# Virtualenvs and node_modules are reinstalled inside the image, never copied.
.venv/
venv/
**/node_modules/

# Build output. `apps/web/dist` in particular must be built by the image, not
# inherited from whatever the developer last ran locally.
**/dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Caches
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Secrets. `.env` is gitignored and must never reach a build context either —
# an image layer is as public as a commit (CLAUDE.md §1.6).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
